        "original_id": "32be01df-887c-5f58-9a64-bfbe5d1dab66",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan, China\n- Mountains: Trivor, The Crown, Momhil Sar\n- Mountain ranges: Karakoram, Hispar Muztagh\n\nFacts:\n- Trivor is one of the high peaks of the Hispar Muztagh subrange of the Karakoram range in Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan.\n- The Crown is also known as Huang Guan Shan and sometimes Crown Peak.\n- The Crown is a mountain in the Karakoram mountain range in China.\n- Momhil Sar is situated in the Hispar Muztagh subrange of the Karakoram range.\n- Momhil Sar lies a few kilometres northwest of its parent peak, Trivor.",
